  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "1. After detergent cleaning, all glassware is rinsed thoroughly with glass-distilled water and then autoclaved."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "2. To 900ml of glass-distilled water are added 100ml of 10X concentrate of CMRL 1066 without glutamine (Gibco Laboratories, GrandIsland, NY, No.330-1540)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "3. Add to the IX CMRL 1066 in the following order:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "4. Adjust pH of medium at 20-25°C to 7.6 with 1 N NaOH."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "5. Add 200ml of 7 percent gelatin (Difco) which had been dissolved in boilinig water."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "6. Sterilize by filtration with air pressure (0.2 μm nitrocellulose, Millipore Corp., Bedford, MA). Store medium at 4°C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "7. Before use, add unheated rabbit serum(\\\"trace hemolyzed\\\"; Pel-Freez Biologicals, Inc., Rogers, AR) to a final concentration of 6 percent."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "8. Dispense to glass or polystyrene tubes or bottles. Fill containers to 50 to 90 percent capacity and captightly.*"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "9. Incubate at 34-37°C"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "*Hamilton, Montana, is at an altitude of 1,200m. At lower elevations the containiers may need to be filled to a higher level."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}